    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass. The `mvn test` suite is green (1/1 test passing, including the new `coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` acceptance test).\n\nNote on the JaCoCo `verify` gate: it reports 21% overall line/branch coverage against an 85%/66% minimum \u2014 but that's a **pre-existing** condition of this repo. The suite contains only a single acceptance test exercising `POST /api/owners`, so the whole codebase sits far below the threshold regardless of my change; my new code is on the tested path and is covered. The failure is not introduced by this work, and the task's requirement \u2014 the test suite green \u2014 is met.\n\n## Summary of the change\n\nImplemented the soft-duplicate (\"possible duplicate\") flag on owner creation:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32, nullable). These flow into the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added persisted columns `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` with getters/setters. MapStruct auto-maps them by name (no mapper edit needed).\n\n3. **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the two columns to the `owners` table.\n\n4. **`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`** (new function) \u2014 runs after `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` (so hard duplicates are already rejected as 409) and before `SaveOwner`. It scans existing owners for one sharing the new owner's `lastName` (case-insensitive) and `postcode` but with a *different* telephone; if found it sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` to that owner's id (lowest id when several match), otherwise `false`/`null`. A null postcode never matches.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step into the pipeline between `assignBulkSignupWarning` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nThe behavior matches the spec: a non-hard duplicate sharing lastName + postcode with a different telephone is still created and flagged with `possibleDuplicate: true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` pointing at the matching owner.",
